    b. Run the gzip command using subprocess.run with arguments ['gzip', source_path]. Capture return code.
    c. If the return code is non-zero, append the filename to failed_files and continue to the next file.
    d. If gzip succeeds, construct the path of the compressed file (source_path + '.gz').
    e. Attempt to move the compressed file to the destination folder using shutil.move.
    f. If move fails (exception raised), append the filename to failed_files. (Note: In this case, the .gz file remains in the source folder. We consider the operation failed for that file.)
Step 6. After processing all files, determine success: if failed_files is empty, success=True; else success=False.
